what is etcd?

etcd is Distributed reliable key value store, it is simple, secure and fast
--
what is key-value store? and how it diff from traditional databases

1)relational db's are strict schema, performs complex query and good in performance, but is very rigid in terms of flexibilty and best for structure data
2)Document store, stores information in from of document each individula information is stored in a document which is a file, these files can be in any format(no schema) and changes to one file will not affect others
Document stores typically stored data in a json format
it is semi structred data, with flexibility offers bit less performance

3)third type of data is simply a key value store, which stores value against a key

key : name
value : John


Key : location
value : New York

Key : user : John
value : name=john,age=45,location=new york,salary=50000

Key : user : John
value : '{"name"="john","age"=45,"location"="new york","salary"=50000}'

value can be a set of properties or json document itself

etcd is one such key value store which is Distributed reliable
