install etcd

1)download binaries
2)extract the binaries
3)Run etcd (./etcd  this command for runnign script)
when you run etcd it starts a servie that listens on port 2379 by default which is etcd server

you would run it a system service or as a pod on a kubernetes cluster

you can then attach any clients to etcd service to store and retrive information
the default client for etcd is etcdctl(etcdctl is command line client for etcd used to execute etcd commands)

./etcdctl put key1 value1
./etcdctl get key1
./etcdctl

